# Target C-II — corrected joint-feasibility O-O path extends through `t<=1.86177`

**Date:** 2026-09-15  
**Status:** proof-only high-`t` endpoint strengthening  
**Scope:** full-core/no-macroscopic-container Type-II branch with `t=(q-k)/D<=1.86177`  
**Dependencies:** corrected joint-feasibility path theorem through `1.8617`; physical opposite-branch argument; phase-free path-region saturation; diameter-path Helly hub  
**Certificate:** `research/verify_target_c_joint_feasible_opposite_branch_path_t186177.py`  
**LEVEL I STATUS:** `STILL OPEN. C-II REMAINS OPEN.`

The corrected low-energy O--O path architecture remains valid almost to its continuous zero-mass endpoint.  At

\[
T={186177\over100000}=1.86177
\]

choose

\[
\lambda={9949\over20000}=0.49745.
\]

The exact outward certificate proves

\[
\boxed{z>2.09606-o(1)},
\]

\[
\boxed{\delta<0.092+o(1)},
\]

and, more precisely, uses

\[
\delta_{max}=0.0912770395\ldots .
\]

The corrected feasibility function satisfies

\[
\boxed{H(2.09606)<-3.9\times10^{-6}},
\]

so the retained-mass lower bound remains nonvacuous with an exact sign margin.

Weighted Markov at the chosen threshold gives

\[
\boxed{P_{low}>0.00033-o(1)},
\]

and one of the at most three dominant phases carries

\[
\boxed{P_{low}^{(j)}>0.00011-o(1)}.
\]

Since retained pair weight per complete train is at most one, that phase contains more than

\[
\boxed{0.00011D-o(D)}
\]

actual O--O complete stopped trains.

The physical same-oriented terminal branch is still impossible.  The exact squared margin is

\[
\boxed{
\left(1-\delta_{max}-{\lambda\over2}\right)^2
-\left(\lambda-{\lambda^2\over4}\right)
>1.14\times10^{-5}.
}
\]

Thus the selected crosscuts use opposite terminal branches, connect the same two separated boundary arcs, and form one simple complement-dual path.  Every path region contains an actual diameter endpoint by the phase-free path-saturation theorem.  The diameter-path Helly theorem supplies one common routing hub, so every nonhub switch is one-sided toward that hub.

If `N_i` is the number of actual diameter intervals starting or stopping at internal boundary `i`, then

\[
\sum_iN_i\le2|H|\le2\pi D+o(D).
\]

After removing the single hub boundary, there are still more than `0.00011D-o(D)` path boundaries.  Since

\[
{2(355/113)\over0.00011}
=57119.87\ldots<57120,
\]

some nonhub strip has

\[
\boxed{N_i\le57119}
\]

for all sufficiently large sources.  Its exact nonzero KKT layer reaction is generated by one or two actual switching diameter bars.

Hence the live corrected path normal form now covers

```text
1.844 < t <= 1.86177:
  z > 2.09606;
  >0.00033 D retained low-energy dominant O-O pair weight;
  >0.00011 D same-phase O-O path trains;
  opposite physical terminal branches;
  every dual path region diameter-loaded;
  one common diameter-routing hub;
  one-sided nonhub switching;
  some nonhub strip has <=57119 moving diameter rows;
  exact reaction generated by <=2 bars.
```

The continuous zero-mass endpoint of this architecture is approximately `1.86179915`; the present theorem stays below it and retains explicit rational/Taylor margins.  No C-II closure is claimed.

**Disposition:** proved proof-only extension of the corrected path/hub/region-saturation/strip normal form through `t<=1.86177`.  C-II and Level I remain open.
